; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   429   *********************************************************************************************************************/
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   430  /*!
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   431   * \brief Checks whether current redundant block can and shall be repaired or not.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   432   * \details We decide between three situations:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   433   *          1. both blocks are valid, nothing to repair
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   434   *          2. both blocks are defect, NvM cannot repair
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   435   *          3. only one block is defect, NvM will try to repair the redundancy
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   436   * \return FALSE block does not have to be repaired or cannot be repaired
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   437   * \return TRUE  block is defect and shall be repaired
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM_Qry.c	   438   * \context TASK
